==Trivia ==
*Shields were first developed during the Bronze Age, as a protection device, designed to block attacks by hand weapons, such as swords, axes and maces, or ranged weapons like sling-stones and arrows. Shields have varied greatly in construction over time and place. Sometimes shields were made of metal, but wood or animal hide construction was much more common; wicker and even turtle shells have been used. Shields were retired in warfare, but are still used to this day for police enforcement.
**The Guards are 1 of 3 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] to have a shield, along with the [[Royal Recruits]] and [[Dark Prince]].
***The Guards are the only troop to have more shield hitpoints than their own hitpoints.
***The Guards are 1 of 2 troops with more damage than hitpoints, the other being [[Wall Breakers]].
**In the Dutch and Russian language settings of the game, the Guards' name translates to "Guardians". In the Turkish, Japanese, and Malaysian language settings of the game, the Guards' name translates to "Protectors", "Shield Warriors", and "Controllers" respectively.
*While not available as a troop in Clash of Clans, the Guards are similar to the Skeletons spawned from a Skeleton Spell.
*The Guards are 1 of 15 [[cards]] associated with [[Skeletons]], with the others being [[Bomber]], [[Skeleton Dragons]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Tombstone]], [[Bomb Tower]], [[Skeleton Army]], [[Witch]], [[Balloon]], [[Giant Skeleton]], Wall Breakers, [[Super Witch]], Graveyard, [[Skeleton King]], and of course, Skeletons.
**In the Chinese language settings of the game, the Guards' name translates to "Skeleton Guards".
*The Guards are tied with Skeletons, [[Bats]], and [[Suspicious Bush]] for the lowest hitpoints of all troops in the game, with 118 hitpoints at Level 15. However, unlike the other two, they also come with a shield.
*The Guards have been featured in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special game modes]] outside of the card. More specifically:
**The Guards are 1 of 23 troops that have been featured in the [[Troop Rush]] game [[:Category:Modes|mode]], the others being Skeletons, Skeleton Dragons, [[Fire Spirit]], Bats, [[Elite Barbarians]], [[Firecracker]], [[Rascals|Rascal Girls]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Heal Spirit]], [[Elixir Golem]], [[Prince]], Balloon, [[Golem]], Wall Breakers, [[Ram Rider]], [[Sparky]], [[Phoenix]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Bandit]], [[Lumberjack]], [[Santa Hog Rider]], and the [[Monk]].
***Along with Skeleton Dragons, the Guards in the Troop Rush game mode would spawn in random positions instead of behind the [[:Category:Crown Towers|Crown Towers]].
**The Guards are 1 of 14 troops that has been featured with a [[Buff#Rage|Rage]] [[buff]], the others being [[Electro Spirit]], [[Giant]], [[Zappies]], Giant Skeleton, [[Goblin Giant]], [[Electro Dragon]], Wall Breakers, [[Electro Giant]], [[Mega Knight]], Ram Rider, [[Electro Wizard]], Sparky, and Royal Ghost.
*They appear to have an underbite, similar to the [[Minions]], Giant Skeleton, [[Lava Hound]], and [[Super Lava Hound]].
*The Guards, along with the Minions, Bomber, Skeletons, Skeleton Dragons, [[Ice Spirit]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A,]] [[Mega Minion]], [[Ice Golem]], [[Dart Goblin]], Elixir Golem, [[Goblin Cage|Goblin Brawler]], [[Baby Dragon]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], Giant Skeleton, Golem, Wall Breakers, [[Bowler]], [[Executioner]], Mega Knight, [[Inferno Dragon]], Royal Ghost, and Lava Hound, are featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Monsters monster] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
**An [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Ice_Guard ice variant] and a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Lava_Guard lava variant] for the Guard are also featured as a monster in Squad Buster.
**According to their description in Squad Busters, the Guards are the [[King's Tower|King']]s bodyguards
*The [[Card Mastery]] task "Pain's An Old Friend" is a reference to a quote mentioned by [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doctor_Strange Dr. Strange].
* The Guards are the subject of an [[Emotes|Emote]].
**The Guard Crown Emote is a reference to the Clash of Clans [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N0QqNGbpTK0&t=631s&pp=ygUQbG9zdCBhbmQgY3Jvd25lZA%3D%3D Lost & Crowned commercial].
*The Guards were featured in the winning [[Battle Decks|deck]] of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/nMANpDweTA4?si=nsUAou7ny3WAA2ve Clash Royale League 2022 Tournament], by a player called Mohamed Light.
*The initial balance change for Guards on the [[Version History#Pass Royale and more (5/5/2025)|May 2025 Update]] was a 6% damage decrease, but it was lowered to 4% [https://royaleapi.com/blog/season-71-balance-wip-may-2025 last minute].

